{
 "_note": "One entry per (family, round): the generator and the review tool of a draft round as they were run, wired to `ga drafts`. family = manifest reload.category = draft check family. `gen`, `review.script`: files of authoring/reload, run from that folder with ROUND_OUT=<out>/<family>/round<N>. `catalog`: module and dict (id -> name or (name, ...)) that lists the round's draft ids. `build`: ids go positional or after `ids_flag`; `takes_flag` passes the takes. `rest`: [gun, gun] pairs and bodies whose rest glbs are made first (rest.py), so parallel generator runs only read them. `seed_ref`: copy smg_ref to <root>/ref (tube and break generators read it). `post`: generator commands after the build. `review.labels`: clip take letters per draft id that the review tool renders (tube round 2: O round 1 pick, C Carnage, T Tactician). `review.pre`: python call before the review. `review.env`: environment of the review commands ({anim_work} is paths.anim_work). `review.takes_flag`: the review tool takes --takes. `review.module`: first argument of the review script. Rounds not listed here are in `unwired`. `archive`: folder (under paths.anim_work) of the archived round this entry reproduces; a round with an archive path is an archived round (a take without an R4 budget is not a stop there, the check reports it as not measurable). `clips_dir`: folder of the clips under the round folder when the generator writes it elsewhere (front3.py: round3-front/clips). `layout` `spec` with `dir` (folder of one draft, {id}): the generator names take and clip in no file name; id, take and body come from the spec. `build.extra`: arguments after the ids. `review_note`: shown instead of a review step when the round has no `review`. `rest_archive`: folder under paths.anim_work holding the rest glbs (<body>/rest_<gun>_R__<gun>_L.glb) the archived round was authored on; copied instead of made by rest.py (rifle rounds 1 and 2: today's rest.py makes other poses). `id_prefix`: only the catalog ids starting with it (round2.py lists the picks of every rifle family). `build.ids_per_take`: ids are passed as <id><take> for every take (round2.py).",
